   <send> element is evaluated", and "if the evaluation of <send>'s arguments
   produces an error, the Processor MUST discard the message without attempting
   to deliver it". So every argument is read here, before any arm runs, and the
   arms below only read the locals this prologue leaves. The first failure is
   one error.execution, the message goes nowhere, and — the error having been
   raised while the element was processed — the block ends (W3C SCXML 4.9).
   A <param> is not one of these: §5.7.1 leaves its pair out and the message
   still goes, which the payload below keeps.

   The whole element is one Go block, so two sends in one action block do not
   declare the same locals twice. #}
{% set send_prologue = model.needs_script_engine and (action.eventexpr or action.targetexpr or action.typeexpr or action.delayexpr or has_namelist or action.idlocation) %}
{% if send_prologue %}
